    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0262" n="212" xml:id="pg212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/243</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-17T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17,
                                1917, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department has received your telegram December 16<anchor n="1" xml:id="d320-f1"/>
                    and Stevens’s December 15. War Department is instructing commander transport <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thomas</hi> not to leave without orders unless ice
                    menaces. <hi rendition="#italic">Thomas</hi> not needed elsewhere at present.
                    Will advise further as to funds for Emerson. Department concurs fully that
                    undesirable interpreters and others should not be allowed to land. Communicate
                    foregoing to Stevens and Emerson and keep Department advised developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
